OneAPI
======

OneAPI is a set of tools for Intel processors and is free to use.
It contains the Intel Fortran compiler and the MKL library.


MKL libary
----------

The MKL library is part of the Intel oneAPI Base toolkit. The MKL library can
be used with Intel Fortran, but also with other compilers such as gfortran and
nagfor.


Intel Fortran
-------------

The Intel Fortran compiler is part of the Intel oneAPI HPC toolkit.
It is available on Windows and Linux, but only on the x86-64 (amd64) processor
architecture. The compiler is called ifx. Use the most recent version of
OneAPI, since ifx is able to compile tfem only recently.


Installation instructions for tfem (minimal installation)
---------------------------------------------------------

- Install Intel Fortran

    Go to site:
       https://www.intel.com/oneapi
    and then go to "Get the toolkits".

    Go to Intel® oneAPI Base Toolkit
    Linux/Web & Local/Online (use online)
    Download file
    cd ~/Downloads
    sudo sh l_BaseKit_p....
    Customized installation
    Only MKL
    Go to Intel® oneAPI HPC Toolkit
    Linux/Web & Local/Online (use online)
    Download file
    cd ~/Downloads
    sudo sh l_HPCKit_p....
    Customized installation
    Only Intel Fortran (for now)
